body:
`%nclusterid` reads make `ptxas` look up the grid dimensions through a constant-memory address derived from the runtime cluster size.

Triton launches clusters with dimensions `(num_ctas, 1, 1)`, so derive `num_programs(0)` from `%nctaid.x / num_ctas` and use `%nctaid.y` and `%nctaid.z` directly. This applies the same launch invariant as #11790.

One observed expansion of `%nclusterid.x` is:

```sass
CS2R.32 R2, SR_CgaSize;
IMAD R2, R2, -0xa0, RZ;
R2UR UR5, R2;
LDCU UR5, c[0x0][UR5+0x2c0];
```

For `num_ctas == 2`, the replacement uses a fixed-offset grid-dimension load and a right shift:

```sass
LDCU UR6, c[0x0][0x370];
USHF.R.U32.HI UR9, URZ, 0x1, UR6;
```

Y and Z each become a fixed-offset load. In two inspected specializations, the generated code loses nine SASS instructions and 128 bytes per specialization, with unchanged register usage and no spills.

